From: Matheus Carvalho <mtw.nda@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: hda/tas2781: restore speaker playback after runtime resume

tas2781_runtime_suspend() mutes the speaker amplifier and clears
playback_started. tas2781_runtime_resume() reloads the DSP program
but never unmutes. System suspend already keeps playback_started, and
system resume unmutes when playback was active.

PipeWire keeps the PCM open while the codec is idle, so the playback
open hook does not run again. After runtime PM the speakers stay
silent on TAS2781 laptops (Lenovo Legion with ALC287, and the same
amplifier on other notebooks) until the PCM is closed and reopened.
HDMI outputs are unaffected because they do not use this amplifier.

Match the system-sleep path: leave playback_started set across runtime
suspend, and unmute after the program reload if playback was active.

Applies to Linux 6.18 as shipped by Manjaro (linux618), including
6.18.32 and 6.18.49. The runtime PM functions are unchanged between
those versions.

Signed-off-by: Matheus Carvalho <mtw.nda@hotmail.com>
---
--- a/sound/hda/codecs/side-codecs/tas2781_hda_i2c.c
+++ b/sound/hda/codecs/side-codecs/tas2781_hda_i2c.c
@@ -742,13 +742,14 @@
 
 	guard(mutex)(&tas_hda->priv->codec_lock);
 
-	/* The driver powers up the amplifiers at module load time.
-	 * Stop the playback if it's unused.
+	/*
+	 * Mute while the amplifier is powered down, but keep playback_started.
+	 * System suspend already does this. Clearing the flag here makes runtime
+	 * resume reload the DSP program and leave the speakers silent when
+	 * userspace keeps the PCM open.
 	 */
-	if (tas_hda->priv->playback_started) {
+	if (tas_hda->priv->playback_started)
 		tasdevice_tuning_switch(tas_hda->priv, 1);
-		tas_hda->priv->playback_started = false;
-	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -763,6 +764,10 @@
 
 	tasdevice_prmg_load(tas_hda->priv, tas_hda->priv->cur_prog);
 
+	/* Program reload comes back muted. Unmute if playback was active. */
+	if (tas_hda->priv->playback_started)
+		tasdevice_tuning_switch(tas_hda->priv, 0);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
